{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "legend",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 0,
			"y": -280,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 210,
			"text": "**Legend**\n🟩 done · 🟨 now · ⬜ taught, not studied · 🟥 not taught yet · 🟪 parked\nCrow updates the colours as blocks close.\n🟧 shaky (see the ⚠ line)"
		},
		{
			"id": "ips1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Definition + classification**\nIP = land / building(s) held for rentals or capital appreciation, NOT owner-use or resale\n3-way split: TAS 40 (IP) vs TAS 16 (PPE, owner-occupied) vs TAS 2 (Inventory, held for sale)\nTraps: undetermined future use → still counts as IP · insignificant ancillary services (security guard) → still IP · significant services (owner-managed hotel) → NOT IP, it's PPE · mixed-use property splits into two only if the portions could be sold separately",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 230
		},
		{
			"id": "ips2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Recognition + initial measurement**\nSame 2-gate test as PPE: ① probable future benefit ② cost reliably measured\nCost = purchase price + directly attributable costs, same acquisition routes as PPE (purchase / deferred payment / lease / exchange / donation) — excludes start-up costs, pre-occupancy operating losses, abnormal waste",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 260,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "ips3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Subsequent measurement — the real exam material**\nEntity picks ONE policy (cost or fair value) for ALL its IP — switching FV→cost is 'highly unlikely' to be allowed under TAS 8\nFair value model: gain/loss straight to P&L every period, no depreciation; don't double-count fixtures/furniture already folded into the FV\nCost model: follow TAS 16 rules + TAS 36 impairment; must still DISCLOSE fair value\nCan't measure FV reliably → rare exception, fall back to cost model, residual assumed zero (mainly matters for IP under construction)",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 470,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 270
		},
		{
			"id": "ips4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Transfers between IP / PPE / inventory — the trap section**\nCost model: transfer changes NOTHING in carrying amount\nFair value model: treated like a REVALUATION — increase → impairment-reversal first, then OCI surplus; decrease → P&L, or eat into an existing surplus first (same order as the PPE revaluation chain already drilled in M2)\nInventory → IP@FV, or construction-complete → IP@FV: the difference goes straight to P&L, no OCI step",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 770,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 230
		},
		{
			"id": "ips5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Derecognition + disclosure**\nGain/loss = proceeds − carrying amount, to P&L (never revenue)\nDisclosure: which model is used, FV reconciliation (fair-value entities), rental income + direct operating expenses split by whether the property earned rent that period — likely light/qualitative on the exam, not a calc block",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1030,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 180
		},
		{
			"id": "ip",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Investment Property (TAS 40)\nSessions 12–13 · 33-slide deck, in hand since 17 Oct, untouched\nReuses the OCI/P&L revaluation mechanics already drilled hard in M2 (see n15–n17 in the M2 map) — the FV-model transfer rules are the same surplus/reversal logic, new label",
			"x": 400,
			"y": 525,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 160
		},
		{
			"id": "cfs1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Objective of financial reporting**\nFor existing/potential investors, lenders, creditors — decisions about buying/selling/holding, lending, voting rights\nAccrual ≠ cash basis — the deck's own exam-shaped examples: revenue recognised on delivery not collection · interest accrues before the quarterly payment is due · bonus expensed when announced, not when paid next Chinese New Year",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1360,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 190
		},
		{
			"id": "cfs2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Qualitative characteristics**\nFundamental (need BOTH): Relevance (predictive/confirmatory value + materiality) + Faithful representation (complete, neutral, free from error — substance over form)\nEnhancing (nice to have): Comparability (≠ Consistency — consistency is the SAME method over time/entities, comparability is the goal that serves) · Verifiability (direct = observe directly e.g. count cash; indirect = recheck the model's inputs and recompute) · Timeliness · Understandability",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1580,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 210
		},
		{
			"id": "cfs3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Financial statements + reporting entity**\nReporting period + at least one prior comparative period + limited forward-looking info (only if it ties to existing assets/liabilities/income/expenses)\nGoing concern — TSA 570 indicators: net liability/current-liability position · capital deficit · debt maturing with no realistic refinance · key management loss · critical supply shortage · intent to liquidate · adverse law change · breach of statutory requirement\nConsolidated (parent + subsidiaries) vs unconsolidated/separate (parent alone) vs combined (no parent-subsidiary link at all)",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 1820,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 250
		},
		{
			"id": "cfs4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Elements of the financial statements**\nAssets = Liabilities + Equity · Income − Expenses\nAsset = present economic resource controlled from past events = right + potential benefit + control (3-part test)\nLiability = present obligation to transfer a resource from a past event — 3 criteria, includes CONSTRUCTIVE obligation (practice/policy, not just contract/law) — same concept as AC311's own Provisions chapter (M1), new label\nIncome = revenue + gains · Expense = expense + losses — 5 classic revenue-recognition trap scenarios (consignment billed-on-consumption · prepaid game-card hours · construction advance for next year's build · sale with 30-day right of return · unused hotel vouchers)",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 2100,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 300
		},
		{
			"id": "cfs5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Recognition + derecognition**\nRecognition = capturing an item that meets an element's definition — NOT every qualifying item actually gets recognised\nDerecognition = removal once it no longer meets the definition (asset: entity loses control · liability: entity no longer has the obligation)",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 2430,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "cfs6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Measurement bases**\nHistorical cost (locked to the transaction-date price, doesn't update except for impairment or a liability becoming onerous) vs Current value: fair value (exit price, orderly market) · value in use / fulfilment value (PV of expected future cash flows) · current cost (entry price, updated to today)",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 2630,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "cfs7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Presentation + disclosure**\nClassification (group by shared nature / function / measurement basis) · Offsetting (generally NOT allowed unless it reflects the real substance) · Profit-or-loss vs OCI split · Aggregation (enough detail to inform, not so much it's noise — the same judgement call disclosure always tests)",
			"x": 900,
			"y": 2830,
			"width": 460,
			"height": 170
		},
		{
			"id": "cf",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Conceptual Framework\nSessions 14–15 · deck landed TODAY (17 Nov), zero drilling\nPure theory/definitions — no numbers, closer to a BA202-shaped paper than the rest of AC311\nExternally sourceable: this IS the IASB Conceptual Framework, identical worldwide — Kieso Ch.2 is a legitimate substitute here, unlike the rest of AC311",
			"x": 400,
			"y": 2100,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 160
		},
		{
			"id": "root",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -80,
			"y": 1425,
			"width": 400,
			"height": 280,
			"text": "# AC311 Final\n25% · **Sat 28 Nov, 09:00**\nSessions 12–15 (last 2 blocks of the Sat/Ajarn Saifon run)\nBoth decks landed 17 Nov: Investment Property (parked since 17 Oct) + Conceptual Framework (added today)\nZero drilling done on either yet"
		},
		{
			"id": "res",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -80,
			"y": 1745,
			"width": 400,
			"height": 260,
			"text": "**Resources**\n⚠ No past-paper match for THIS year's final scope — the Drive's `final 2021.pdf` covers impairment, which sits in THIS year's Midterm 2, not the final. Investment Property + Conceptual Framework have no past-paper proxy found yet — worth checking the Drive again or asking a senior directly.\nBoth decks now on disk: `Investment property_October 2026 (1).pptx` (33 slides) · `Framework financial reporting_2026.pdf` (added 17 Nov).",
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
